   was devised -- informally --
   _before_ the Feds took it over.  Anybody want to go into the story in
   detail?  Did someone when I wasn't looking?  (Did I??)

The Feds used WW I as an excuse to regulate the EM spectrum (or
significantly increase their regulation), I gather.  What might be
interesting in this case is to probe for what seems to be one of the
"weak spots" in self-regulating communities -- differing user groups
with strongly differing interests.  For instance, it wouldn't be
surprising if broadcasters could self-regulate reasonably well,
because they all have the "same interests" in the long run, but when
the broadcasters and the people owning trucking fleets try to split
the spectrum between themselves, the game has enough zero-sum nature
for self-regulation to be much less stable.

