I like the point about short-circuiting reproductive instincts through birth
control.  My summary is that it evolved to work as follows:

     -> have sexual intercourse because of inborn desires
          -> bear child
               -> nurture child from instinct

and has become

     -> have sex because of inborn desires but no child because of birth
        control, hence no bridge to child-nurturing instinct

This model suggests that we'd have less of a self-genociding problem among
high-tech populations if the act of having a child was in itself an inborn
desire.

Note that I oversimplify by leaving out memetic selection.  We'll need to be
sure to incorporate philoprogenitivity into our future memetically engineered
religions and philosophies.
